# P2 — line-ending normalisation.
#
# The repo accumulated a 21 141-insertion / 21 141-deletion phantom diff purely
# because some checkouts wrote CRLF and others LF. `text=auto eol=lf` keeps the
# working tree, the index and every platform in agreement, so `git status` only
# ever shows real changes.
#
# After this file lands, a one-time renormalisation is required:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "Normalise line endings (P2)"
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only helper scripts keep CRLF so they stay runnable in cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never diff, never convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfiles and generated model output must diff as text for review.
# (Deliberately NOT marked -diff: lockfile changes must stay reviewable.)
package-lock.json text eol=lf
docs/data-room/FINANCIAL_MODEL.csv text eol=lf
docs/data-room/CARBON_EXPORT.json text eol=lf
